---
title: Beef Bourguignon
servings: 6
prepTime: 30 min
cookTime: 1 hr 15 min
source:
  name: foodnetwork.com
  url: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/ina-garten/beef-bourguignon-recipe-1942045
tags: Alcohol, Beef
---

Preheat the oven to 250°F.

Heat the @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large #Dutch oven{}.
Add the @bacon{8%oz}(good quality, diced) and cook over medium heat for ~{10%minutes},
stirring occasionally, until the bacon is lightly browned.
Remove the bacon with a slotted spoon to a large plate.

Cut a @beef chuck roast{2 1/2%pounds} into 1" cubes.
Dry the beef cubes with paper towels and then sprinkle them with @salt and @pepper.
In batches in single layers, sear the beef in the hot oil for 3 to 5 minutes, turning to brown on all sides.
Remove the seared cubes to the plate with the bacon and continue searing until all the beef is browned.
Set aside.

Toss the @carrots{1%lb}(sliced diagonally into 1" chunks) and @yellow onions{2}(sliced)
with @salt{1%tbsp} and @pepper{2%tsp} in the fat in the pan and cook for ~{10-15%minutes},
stirring occasionally, until the onions are lightly browned.

Add the @garlic{2%cloves}(chopped or minced) and cook for 1 more minute.
Add the @Cognac{1/2%cup}, stand back, and ignite with a match to burn off the alcohol.

Put the meat and bacon back into the pot with the juices.
Add the bottle of @dry red wine{750%ml}(such as Cote du Rhone or Pinot Noir) plus enough @beef broth{2%cup} to almost cover the meat.
Add the @tomato paste{1%tbsp} and @thyme{1%tsp}(fresh).

Bring to a simmer, cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and place it in the oven for about ~{75%min}
or until the meat and vegetables are very tender when pierced with a fork.
Remove the pan from the oven.

Combine @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}(at room temperature) and the @all-purpose flour{3%tbsp}
with a fork and stir into the stew.
Add the @frozen whole onions{1%lb}.

Saute the @mushrooms{1%lb}(fresh, stems discarded, caps thickly sliced) in @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}
for ~{10%minutes} until lightly browned and then add to the stew.
Bring the stew to a boil on top of the stove, then lower the heat and simmer for ~{15%minutes}. Season to taste.

= Serving =
To serve, toast the @Country bread or Sour Dough{} in the toaster or oven.
Rub each slice on 1 side with a cut clove of @garlic{1%clove}.

For each serving, spoon the stew over a slice of bread and sprinkle with @parsley{}(finely chopped).

